  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. Your Final Project - The Brief</h2>
    <p>Imagine a real client comes to you:</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Client Brief:</b> "Hi, I am Ahmed. I have a shop in Lahore - Fresh Mart. I sell Fruits, Vegetables, and Dairy. I want a website where customers can see my products, filter by category, add to cart, and order on WhatsApp. My budget is Rs. 25,000. I need it in 5 days."<br><br>This is a REAL freelancing job. Today you will build exactly this website. After this lesson, you can take real jobs like this.</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - Final Project - Fresh Mart Shop</h2>
    <p>Try it - Filter, Search, Add to Cart, Order on WhatsApp. This is your target:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
      <div class="shop">
        <div class="shop-nav"><b>🥦 Fresh Mart - Lahore</b><span>🛒 Cart: <b id="shopCartCount">0</b> items | Rs. <b id="shopCartTotal">0</b></span></div>
        <div class="shop-hero"><h3 style="margin:0">Fresh Fruits, Vegetables & Dairy 🥦</h3><p style="margin:6px 0">Delivered Fresh in 1 Hour - Lahore Only</p><input class="demo-input" id="shopSearch" placeholder="Search - e.g. Mango, Milk, Apple..." oninput="renderShop()" style="max-width:360px;margin:0 auto"></div>
        <div style="text-align:center;padding:12px 0 0"><button class="filter-btn active" id="shopAll" onclick="shopFilter('all')">All</button><button class="filter-btn" id="shopFruits" onclick="shopFilter('fruits')">🍎 Fruits</button><button class="filter-btn" id="shopVeg" onclick="shopFilter('veg')">🥕 Vegetables</button><button class="filter-btn" id="shopDairy" onclick="shopFilter('dairy')">🥛 Dairy</button></div>
        <div class="shop-grid" id="shopGrid"></div>
        <div class="cart-box"><b>🛒 Your Cart</b><div id="shopCartList" style="font-size:14px;color:#475569;margin:6px 0">Cart is empty. Add products above.</div><button class="btn" style="width:100%" onclick="shopCheckout()">Order on WhatsApp 📱</button><p id="shopOrderMsg" style="text-align:center;color:#16a34a;font-weight:bold;margin-top:8px"></p></div>
        <div style="background:#0f172a;color:#cbd5e1;text-align:center;padding:12px;font-size:13px">© 2026 Fresh Mart Lahore | 📱 0300-1234567 | Free Delivery Over Rs. 1000</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h2>3. 5 Steps - How Professionals Build Any Website</h2>
    <div class="steps"><div class="step"><b>1️⃣</b>Brief<br>Ask client: What? For whom? Goal?</div><div class="step"><b>2️⃣</b>Plan<br>Draw boxes on paper</div><div class="step"><b>3️⃣</b>Design<br>Colors, fonts, layout</div><div class="step"><b>4️⃣</b>Code<br>HTML + CSS + JS</div><div class="step"><b>5️⃣</b>Test & Launch<br>Mobile, links, form</div></div>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Step</th><th>What to Do</th><th>Time</th></tr>
      <tr><td>1. Brief</td><td>Ask: What do you sell? Who are customers? What should website DO? - Sell, show, contact?</td><td>30 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2. Plan</td><td>Draw sections on paper - Navbar, Hero, Products, Cart, Footer. List all products + prices.</td><td>30 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>3. Design</td><td>Pick 2 colors + 1 font. Fresh Mart = Green + Dark. Food = Red + Yellow. School = Blue + White.</td><td>1 hour</td></tr>
      <tr><td>4. Code</td><td>Build section by section. Test after each section. Do not code all at once.</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr>
      <tr><td>5. Test & Launch</td><td>Check on mobile, all buttons, cart, WhatsApp order. Show client, fix, launch.</td><td>1 day</td></tr>
    </table>
    <h2>4. Cart Logic - The Heart of Shop Website</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let products = [</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">{ name: "Mango", price: 250, type: "fruits", emoji: "🥭" },</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">{ name: "Milk 1L", price: 220, type: "dairy", emoji: "🥛" },</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">{ name: "Potato 1kg", price: 120, type: "veg", emoji: "🥔" }</span><br>
<span class="text">];</span><br><br>
<span class="text">let cart = []; // Empty cart - Array of products user adds</span><br><br>
<span class="text">function addToCart(index) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">cart.push(products[index]); // Add product to cart</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">updateCart(); // Show new cart</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="text">function updateCart() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let total = 0;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">for (let item of cart) { total += item.price; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("cartCount").innerText = cart.length;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("cartTotal").innerText = total;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// WhatsApp Order - Open WhatsApp with order text</span><br>
<span class="text">function checkout() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let msg = "Hi Fresh Mart! I want to order: ";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">for (let item of cart) { msg += item.name + " - Rs. " + item.price + ", "; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">window.open("https://wa.me/923001234567?text=" + encodeURIComponent(msg));</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>5. Search + Filter - Together</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">function showProducts() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let search = document.getElementById("search").value.toLowerCase();</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let html = "";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">for (let i = 0; i < products.length; i++) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let p = products[i];</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let matchSearch = p.name.toLowerCase().includes(search);</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let matchFilter = (filter === "all" || p.type === filter);</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (matchSearch && matchFilter) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">html += `&lt;div&gt;${p.emoji} ${p.name} - Rs. ${p.price} &lt;button onclick="addToCart(${i})"&gt;Add&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/div&gt;`;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("grid").innerHTML = html;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <p><b>Logic:</b> Show product ONLY if it matches BOTH - Search AND Filter. If search is empty, <code>includes("")</code> is true for all - So all show. Clever!</p>
    <h2>6. Before Launch - Final Checklist ✅</h2>
    <p>Tick all before you send to client:</p>
    <p>✅ Works on mobile - No horizontal scroll, buttons big enough<br>✅ All images load - No broken image icon<br>✅ All buttons work - Add to cart, filter, search, WhatsApp<br>✅ No spelling mistakes<br>✅ Prices correct - Ask client to check all prices<br>✅ Contact number correct - Test WhatsApp link yourself<br>✅ Footer has shop name + phone + address</p>
    <h2>7. Homework - Build YOUR Final Project</h2>
    <p>You have 5 days. Choose ONE and build fully in Playground, then deploy in Lesson 47:</p>
    <p>1. <b>Shop Website</b> - Like Fresh Mart - 12 products, 3 categories, search, filter, cart, WhatsApp order<br>2. <b>Restaurant Website</b> - Menu with prices, cart, order on WhatsApp, reviews<br>3. <b>School Website</b> - Courses, teachers, admission form, fee calculator<br>4. <b>Your Portfolio + Shop Combined</b> - Your services with prices + order form</p>
    <p>After building, send link to 3 friends + 1 shop owner. Ask: "Would you pay for this?" - If yes, you are ready for freelancing (Lesson 48).</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Professional Process = Brief → Plan → Design → Code → Test → Launch | Cart = Array + push() + total loop | Filter + Search = Show only if BOTH match | WhatsApp Order = wa.me/number?text= + encodeURIComponent(message) | Test on mobile before launch | Ask client to check prices + phone number</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> <a href="/lesson46">Lesson 46 - SEO Basics</a> - Make your website appear on Google. Title, description, keywords, speed.</p>
